                        "entry_id": "0ffbba09-2e84-359b-a44e-383d2f8ce040",
                        "glosses": [
                            "That has passed; bygone."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f91c9cca-f41b-48bf-9e92-304cefd3f733",
                                "sense_id": "e3955440-2d6e-3308-a1a0-73dca3fcb09a",
                                "text": "Which my liege Lady seeing, thought it best\n[…]all forepast displeasures to repeale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff493e8d-f43f-42d2-9e69-7b2abb706030",
                                "sense_id": "e3955440-2d6e-3308-a1a0-73dca3fcb09a",
                                "text": "Of that condition is this other counsell, which Philosophie giveth, onely to keepe forepast [translating passé] felicities in memorie, and thence blot out such griefes as we have felt[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "11597868-5f30-4710-ae4b-b7c52303ef40",
                                "sense_id": "e3955440-2d6e-3308-a1a0-73dca3fcb09a",
                                "text": "Take him away,\n My fore-past proofes, how ere the matter fall\n Shall taze my feares of little vanitie,\n Hauing vainly fear'd too little."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
